import java.util.Scanner;

public class OverloadSeries {

    // Overloaded method 1: S = x/1 + x^2/2 + x^3/3 + ... + x^n/n
    public void series(int x, int n) {
        double sum = 0.0;
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            sum += Math.pow(x, i) / (double) i;
        }
        System.out.printf("Series 1 Sum (x=%d, n=%d) = %.4f\n", x, n, sum);
    }

    // Overloaded method 2: S = 1 + (1+2) + (1+2+3) + ... + (1+2+...+n)
    public void series(int n) {
        long totalSum = 0;
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            long termSum = 0;
            for (int j = 1; j <= i; j++) {
                termSum += j;
            }
            totalSum += termSum;
        }
        System.out.println("Series 2 Sum (n=" + n + ") = " + totalSum);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        OverloadSeries obj = new OverloadSeries();

        System.out.print("Enter value of x for Series 1: ");
        int x = sc.nextInt();
        System.out.print("Enter value of n for Series 1: ");
        int n1 = sc.nextInt();

        System.out.print("Enter value of n for Series 2: ");
        int n2 = sc.nextInt();

        System.out.println("\n--- RESULTS ---");
        obj.series(x, n1);
        obj.series(n2);
        sc.close();
    }
}
```

### Variable Description Table (VDT):

| Variable Name | Data Type | Purpose / Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `x` | `int` | Parameter storing the base value for Series 1 |
| `n` | `int` | Parameter storing the number of terms for series calculation |
| `sum` | `double` | Accumulator storing the sum of terms in Series 1 |
| `i` | `int` | Loop index for iterating through terms 1 to `n` |
| `totalSum` | `long` | Accumulator for the overall sum of Series 2 |
| `termSum` | `long` | Computes the sub-sum (1 + 2 + ... + i) in Series 2 |
| `j` | `int` | Inner loop counter to compute sub-series terms in Series 2 |
| `n1`, `n2` | `int` | Store user inputs for terms in `main()` |
| `obj` | `OverloadSeries` | Object reference to call overloaded methods |

